# Build-context filter for the PARENT-context build (docker-compose.yml sets
# `context: ..` so the Dockerfile can COPY the sibling juena-core source).
#
# Docker looks for `<dockerfile>.dockerignore` first and only falls back to a
# `.dockerignore` at the context root. The context root here is the parent
# directory, which has none -- so this file is the ONLY filter in effect.
# Anything missing here is sent to the daemon.
#
# That parent directory holds roughly nine gigabytes across a dozen unrelated
# repositories, several of which contain real credentials in their own `.env`,
# including the first-generation `Vitess-AI-Agent` checkout. So the rule is
# deny-by-default: exclude every top-level entry, re-admit only the two
# directories this image is built from, then prune inside them.
#
# The re-admission below names this repository's directory as it sits on disk.
# Renaming the checkout breaks the build; the Dockerfile's COPY paths carry the
# same name, so both change together.

# 1. Everything in the parent, including unrelated repositories and the
#    first-generation Vitess-AI-Agent checkout.
*

# 2. The two directories the build reads, and nothing else.
!Vitess-AI-Agent-v2
!juena-core

# 3. Prune inside them. Order matters: these follow the re-admissions above, and
#    for any given path the last matching pattern wins.

# Credentials. Nothing reads .env from the image; Compose supplies the
# environment at run time.
**/.env
**/.env.*
**/*.pem
**/*.key
**/*.crt

# Version control and virtual environments. The .venv directories are hundreds
# of megabytes each and are rebuilt inside the image by `uv sync`.
**/.git
**/.gitignore
**/.gitattributes
**/.gitmodules
**/.venv
**/venv
**/node_modules

# Python build, test and tool output.
**/__pycache__
**/*.py[cod]
**/*.egg-info
**/.pytest_cache
**/.coverage
**/htmlcov
**/.claude
**/.ruff_cache
**/.mypy_cache
**/.ipynb_checkpoints
**/build
**/dist

# Tests. The Dockerfile copies no test suite; excluding them keeps the context
# small and keeps this honest about what ships.
Vitess-AI-Agent-v2/tests
Vitess-AI-Agent-v2/rag/vitess-rag/tests
juena-core/tests
juena-core/examples
juena-core/scripts

# Runtime state and local data. The project directory and the Chroma index are
# Docker volumes at run time, and a VITESS build produced on the host is not the
# one this image runs -- stage 1 builds its own.
Vitess-AI-Agent-v2/data
Vitess-AI-Agent-v2/rag/vitess-rag/chroma_db
Vitess-AI-Agent-v2/rag/vitess-rag/data/chroma*
Vitess-AI-Agent-v2/vitess
Vitess-AI-Agent-v2/MODULES
**/*.db
**/*.sqlite
**/*.log
**/logs

# Editor and OS noise.
**/.DS_Store
**/.vscode
**/.idea
**/*.swp
